shanxi and the ten rings brought dragons  to the marvel cinematic universe and  left people wanting more whether they're  androids or demons from the moon these  dragons fascinate as friends foes or  both these are the biggest dragons from  marvel comics that we want to see in the  mcu  finn fang fume is one of the most  enduring monsters in the marvel universe  created by stan lee and jack kirby in  1961's strange tales number 89 he was  later incorporated into marvel  continuity and is a cross media  superstar appearing in comics cartoons  and video games finn fang fume is so  familiar to marvel fans that the glimpse  of a massive underwater dragon in the  shanghai trailers led to wild  speculation that we now know didn't pay  off finn fang fume is an alien from the  far-off world of kakarothara and when  he's introduced lies dormant in an  underground temple a scholar familiar  with finfun's legend awakens him hoping  to turn him against the invading forces  of communist china leading to a wall  whipping ship-smashing chase worthy of  looney tunes at its most chaotic finn  fang boom's history in the marvel  universe almost defies description he's  fought iron man squirrel girl and thanks  to an inter-company crossover the  justice league of america he's converted  to buddhism been a chef and lived on  monster isle he's even saved christmas  all that's left for this enduring comic  book character is a long overdue  appearance in the marvel cinematic  universe  ask any marvel fan which classic  fantastic four villains they want to see  in the mcu and odds are they'll name  heavy hitters like dr doom and galactus  but if the mcu wants to introduce an ffo  never before seen on screen why not dig  a little deeper into the rose gallery  why not introduce  dragon man joining finn fang fume in the  very exclusive dragon in the little  purple pants club dragon man first  appeared in 1965's fantastic four number  35 an android created by professor  gregson gilbert and brought to life by  the evil alchemist diablo dragon man was  unleashed on the fantastic four during  their visit to state university he was a  creature of powerful strength and  rudimentary intelligence until in true  king kong fashion a beautiful blonde  sue storm soothed the savage beast  brawling his way across the marvel  universe he spot spider-man the hulk and  even the pint-sized heroes of power pack  but after sue and reed's daughter  valeria richards upgraded his  programming he became a valued member of  the future foundation  i was a force in the cosmos before the  worlds were made i have brought whole  civilizations low but do you really  expect to stand against the dragon of  the moon  so boasted the eldritch horror  imprisoned on titan in the new defenders  number 138 the dragon of the moon is a  demon whose corrosive influence can  compel others to do evil deeds to give  an idea of its power it once claimed  thanos as one of its disciples when the  youngest sci talent heather douglas  trained on titan to unlock her mental  abilities the dragon attempted to take  over her mind believing she had defeated  it heather assumed the name moondragon  as a symbol of pride in actuality the  dragon of the moon was slowly corrupting  her years later it successfully turned  moon dragon against the defenders  unleashing a threat that only ended  after several of her teammates  sacrificed their lives with its ability  to corrupt the seemingly incorruptible  the dragon of the moon would be a  terrifying villain in the mcu one  possible path toward the mcu is  surprisingly clear in the comics heather  douglas is the daughter of traxx the  destroyer and a member of the guardians  of the galaxy in her own right if  moondragon joins the on-screen guardians  can the dragon of the moon be lurking  far behind  unlike the other marvel dragons on this  list xiaolao the undying has technically  already appeared in the mcu if you count  a single pair of red eyes glowing in the  dark introduced in marvel premiere  number 16 xiao lao is an ancient dragon  who dwells in the mystical city of  kunlun and is the power source behind  the iron fist mythos a warrior must  defeat xiaolao the undying whose molten  heart is hidden inside a sacred cavern  if they are to absorb his power and  become iron fist included in this heroic  lineage is the modern day iron fist  danny rent but when the 2017 iron fist  television show on netflix welcomed rand  and kunlun into the mcu xiaolao was  nowhere to be seen though he was  mentioned by name xiaolao never made a  full appearance due to one disappointing  factor  the budget  as for danny rand himself finn jones  told a reporter in 2017 i'd love to have  the budget for these shows to have a  full-on game of thrones style dragon but  unfortunately you know we have budget  restraints that's the nature of the show  netflix's iron fist ended in 2018 after  two seasons but the character's rich  comic book history is still worth  exploring and xiaolao is still somewhere  out there in the darkness waiting for  his close-up superhero comics generally  make bad playgrounds for babies if  you're a baby in a superhero comic maybe  you'll be lucky like cable and be sent  into the future to become a grizzled  cybernetic warrior or you could be like  shogo lee and turn into a dragon  orphaned by a meteor crash and adopted  by x-men and former mall rat jubilee  shogo is a seemingly ordinary baby  having the x-men for godparents  automatically guaranteed shogo a life of  adventure but fate had a big surprise  for jubilee when she brought shogo  through a magical gate into the realm of  otherworld in excalibur volume four  number two fairy magic combined with the  unlimited power of a child's imagination  spontaneously turned shogo into a giant  fire-breathing dragon now the youngest  member of excalibur shogu acts as  transportation and defense for his  mother and their teammates while in  otherworld shogu the dragon would be an  adorable addition to the mcu but watch  out for those explosive tantrums  before the dawn of the superhero there  was  grog one of finfang fumes strange tales  fraternity brothers grog first appears  in strange tales number 83 as a member  of an ancient dragon race held back by  the great wall of china in the spirit of  creature features like gamera and the  deadly mantis the prehistoric beast  spends thousands of years sleeping  beneath polar ice until nuclear testing  behind the iron curtain startles him in  his second appearance grog boards a  soviet rocket ship destined for mars  seemingly ending his fire breathing  threat forever the 2005 comic marvel  monsters monsters on the prowl number  one revealed that grog had been seized  by the collector becoming part of his  macabre menagerie along with other  missing silverage comic book behemoths  like taboo and grodu though grog's city  smashing days were far from over  memorably played by benicio del toro the  collector is one of the most slippery  supporting characters in the marvel  cinematic universe the true depths of  his specimen collection are unknown  could grog be among them if nothing else  it would be fun to see grog and giant  man doing the mcu version of godzilla vs  kong  mr lao a once mortal man who gained  eternal life after a curse transformed  him into a lung dragon did the only  sensible thing with his immortality he  got a job acting as the advisor for the  atlas foundation mr lau utilized  centuries of experience to become a  master strategist with the added perk of  ritually devouring every atlas  foundation leader after the appointment  of their successor mr lau would  eventually grant his services to agent  of atlas jimmy wu though the only agenda  he truly follows is his own laos  machiavellian intelligence sets him  apart from the more bestial members of  this list and he would be an intriguing  addition to any upcoming mcu film or  television series plus after randall  park's scene stealing turn as agent  jimmy wu in ant-man and the wasp and one  division who wouldn't want to see him  trade quips with a colossal dragon  that's worth a try  flying past the finish line is the  x-men's diminutive dragon friend  lockheed debuting in uncanny x-men  number 166 by chris claremont and paul  smith lockheed is a member of the alien  race known as the flock with the x-men  trapped in space during the brood saga  lockheed rescued kitty pryde by torching  the brood aliens hunting her  accompanying the x-men back to earth  lockheed helped kitty fight off more  alien hatchlings and a beautiful  friendship was born given his small size  lockheed is often regarded as a pet but  he is highly intelligent and  communicates in several languages  including english apart from the x-men  he has worked with sword guarded the  time gem with the pet avengers and  squared off against fellow dragon finn  fangfun lockheed can usually be found  perched upon kitty's shoulder whether  they're dimension hopping with excalibur  in the crosstime caper or sailing the  high seas in marauders lockheed had a  cameo in the new mutants the final fox  x-men film alongside magic kitty's comic  book best friend but after the failure  of the new mutants at the box office it  would be a shame to consign lockheed to  cinematic limbo marvel studios plans for  the x-men remain unknown but if kitty  pride appears in the mcu as either the  wide-eyed junior x-men or the  swashbuckling captain kate lockheed is  sure to be flying by her side  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel comics characters  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one
 

